WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.180
In the early 1800s, Thomas Young's
experiments showed light making interference

2
00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.340
fringes.

3
00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.000
Only a wave model could explain them.

4
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.450
Within a few decades, the
wave model was accepted.

5
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.660
By 1900, light as a wave
seemed settled science.

6
00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:20.100
So which experiment made
physicists think again?

7
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.430
In this mission, you'll test what a wave
model of light really predicts against

8
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.830
what experiments actually show.

9
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.930
Then you'll pick out the results
that no wave model can explain.

10
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:36.270
Your mission: find out which experiment
made physicists think again about light,

11
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.560
and explain why.
